{"author":{"id":"d4d77c46d796577aec35d160aa1e09aa095720b03e93f3ca34ad3c079140e2fb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794735275,"nonce":"3646TDPude4nmgKBvlc/e7Vz78w=","title":"MSL_SLOTS does not give each entry point's MSL function name","message":"Naga renames entry points whose WGSL names MSL reserves: hxnsl's `vertex`, `fragment` and `main` become the MSL functions `vertex_`, `fragment_` and `main_`. A Metal driver needs those names for `newFunctionWithName`, and today hxn-gpu-metal's README and skill document the suffix instead of reading it.\n\nnaga's MSL writer returns them (`TranslationInfo::entry_point_names`), and russl's `targets::emit` drops that value. The fix is in russl: carry the name in `reflection.native.msl` (a `function` field on `MslEntry`), then hxnsl adds it to each `MSL_SLOTS` entry. russl changes go through Blinc's session.","files":null}]}